MongoDB Configuration and Development
1. Overview
MongoDB will be used as the primary application database for AI-FAO-Assistant.

MongoDB can store:

Farmer profiles

Farm information

Crop information

Conversations

Chat messages

Crop observations

Disease observations

Weather records

Market records

AI interaction logs

The architecture becomes:

                    AI-FAO-Assistant
                           |
                     FastAPI Backend
                           |
                 +---------+---------+
                 |                   |
             AI Layer            MongoDB
                 |                   |
          +------+-------+     +-----+------+
          |      |       |     |            |
         LLM    RAG    Tools Farmers       Crops
          |      |             |            |
          |   Vector DB        Farms    Conversations
          |                    |
          +--------------------+

MongoDB is the application database. A vector database or MongoDB's vector-search capabilities can be added separately for the RAG layer.

2. MongoDB Architecture
Recommended database:

MongoDB
  |
  └── aifao
       |
       ├── farmers
       ├── farms
       ├── crops
       ├── conversations
       ├── messages
       ├── observations
       ├── diseases
       ├── weather
       ├── market_prices
       ├── documents
       └── ai_logs

MongoDB stores JSON-like BSON documents.

For example, a farmer document can look like:

{
  "_id": "ObjectId(...)",
  "name": "Farmer Name",
  "phone": "+91XXXXXXXXXX",
  "language": "ta",
  "location": {
    "type": "Point",
    "coordinates": [80.2707, 13.0827]
  },
  "created_at": "2026-09-30T00:00:00Z"
}

