21. Farm Location
MongoDB supports GeoJSON-style location data.

Example:

{
  "location": {
    "type": "Point",
    "coordinates": [
      80.2707,
      13.0827
    ]
  }
}

Important:

coordinates[0] = longitude
coordinates[1] = latitude

Create a geospatial index:

farms_collection.create_index(
    [
        ("location", "2dsphere")
    ]
)

This allows future features such as:

Farmer
   |
   v
Farm coordinates
   |
   v
Nearby weather
   |
   v
Nearby markets
   |
   v
Regional agricultural information

